  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Unshakeable NATO commitment and UK nuclear deterrent; Strategic Defence Review and path to 2.5% of GDP; Martyn’s Law. Secure borders via a Border Security Command, smashing smuggler gangs, fast‑track returns, and a UK–EU security pact. Neighbourhood Policing Guarantee, tougher knife‑crime measures, and a plan to halve violence against women and girls. Strict fiscal rules with OBR oversight; cap corporation tax at 25% and permanent full expensing; keep taxes on working people low. Make Brexit work with better EU ties; support for Ukraine and AUKUS; clear‑eyed China strategy.\nTEXT_C: Sign the Nuclear Ban Treaty, cancel Trident, and reform NATO toward de‑escalation and no‑first‑use. End Prevent and the hostile environment; humane asylum with safe routes and right to work. Wealth tax on assets over £10m, align capital gains with earnings, 10:1 pay ratios, pathway to Universal Basic Income, and public ownership of rail, water and Big 5 energy firms. Rent controls and end Right to Buy; frequent‑flyer levy and halt new road‑building.",
  "reasoning": "Given the electorate’s higher weighting on authority, proportionality, and loyalty, TEXT_E’s emphases on defense and policing, secure borders, fiscal rules, and stable pro‑business taxation better match those priorities while still addressing care. TEXT_C leans more toward equality and sanctity and explicitly downplays traditional authority and national defense (e.g., canceling Trident, NATO de‑escalation), making it less aligned with the profile.",
